{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And behold, it has turned the hair white, and there is a quick raw flesh in the swelling.</b> The meaning of this verse is not that both of them are required — white hair and raw flesh — for Scripture declared white hair alone impure in the first section, and likewise raw flesh alone is a sign of impurity. If so, its meaning is: and it has turned the hair white, <i>or</i> there is a quick raw flesh in the swelling. And He mentioned white hair in the swelling [שְׂאֵת] even though He had already mentioned it in the bright spot [בַּהֶרֶת], to teach that in both of them it is a sign of impurity."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:19.409292097Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}